Newspeak House Booking Policy

1. Purpose
This policy sets out a single, clear process for booking spaces at Newspeak House for events.
The booking system is meant to make access to Newspeak House spaces clear and predictable, while still letting Faculty and Fellowship Candidates use the house informally.
Faculty and Fellowship Candidates are welcome to use Newspeak House spaces on an ad hoc basis. However, anyone who needs exclusive use of a space must record it as a booking.

2. Technology and Administration
Newspeak House will use Libre Booking as the system for managing bookings and booking requests:
https://2026.newspeak.house/booking/Web/dashboard.php
The Record Keepers are responsible for administering Libre Booking and for its technical running. If something goes wrong with the system, the Record Keepers are responsible for fixing it in a timely manner. They are also responsible for ensuring all candidates and Faculty have access to a working account and full access to the system as described in the below document. 

3. What Counts as a Booking?
A booking is an arrangement for the exclusive use of a Newspeak House space for a defined period of time.
Exclusive use means the person running the booked event may ask anyone else using the space to leave for the duration of the booking.
Each booking should include a short description of the activity or event. A few sentences explaining what the space will be used for is normally enough.
Bookings should be made through Libre Booking.

4. Who Can Book?
Bookings are paid for with booking credits. One credit pays for one hour in any regular space, whichever space it is.
Fellowship Candidates receive 50 booking credits per month.
Faculty members receive 30 booking credits per month.
Credits belong to the month in which the booking takes place, not the month in which it is made. You can book ahead using a future month's credits. For example, in October you can book sessions in December using your December credits. Unused credits do not roll over and expire at the end of their month.

Sponsored bookings
Other individuals or organisations may request use of Newspeak House spaces where appropriate. Such bookings need a sponsor, who can be either a faculty member or a Fellowship Candidate. The sponsor must agree to spend their own booking credits on the booking.
The sponsor is responsible for the event and must attend it for its full duration. With mutual consent, the sponsor may nominate another Fellowship Candidate or Faculty member to take over this responsibility. That person must then attend for the full duration instead.

5. Regular Spaces
Booking credits apply to the following regular Newspeak House spaces:
Terrace
Committee Room
Library
Lounge / Kitchen

These spaces are allocated on a first-come, first-served basis: the first booking recorded in Libre Booking takes priority. Members may negotiate with each other, and a member may choose to give up their booking.

6. Cancellations
If a booking is cancelled more than seven days before it is due to start, all of its credits are refunded.
If a booking is cancelled within seven days of its start, the credits are not refunded.

7. Booker Responsibilities
The person responsible for a booking (the booker, or for a sponsored booking the sponsor or their nominee) must:
clean up the space after use
manage noise during the booking
make sure the event finishes at a reasonable time
listen to and respond to residents' concerns

8. Guest Rooms
Guest rooms will be governed by a separate Guest Room Policy, and the booking-credit system in this policy does not apply to them.
Until a Guest Room Policy is established, a guest room can only be used by a Fellowship Candidate who makes a request through the usual 48-hour lazy consensus process.

9. Event Space
The Event Space is governed by the college. Our relationship with the college over it will be set out in a separate Event Space Policy.
Until an Event Space Policy is established, Fellowship Candidates should post requests for the Event Space in the agent-communications channel. The agent will pass them directly to Ed for consideration.

